guide.nexustech.unsupported=Special recipe: grid unavailable
guide.nexustech.tap=Tap icons to see names. Alternatives cycle automatically.
guide.nexustech.ingredient_missing=No ingredient alternatives are registered in this installation; the recipe may be unavailable.
guide.nexustech.lesson.0=In Contents, choose a chapter and use arrows to browse the list or pages. Double arrows go to the beginning or end; in Recipes they skip ten results. Search by name or ID and tap items to identify them.
guide.nexustech.lesson.1=Start with an energy source: the coal generator accepts furnace fuel; the lava generator uses a lava bucket. Connect your source to machines using energy cables. The battery stores energy.
guide.nexustech.lesson.2=The basic solar panel generates during the day with a clear sky. The electric turbine needs flowing vanilla water in an adjacent block. Search for each part by name under Recipes.
guide.nexustech.lesson.3=Nexus 3x3 solar array: craft 1 controller, 2 poles and 9 modules. Place the controller at the bottom, stack the 2 poles above it, and build a 3x3 layer of modules centered above the pole. Modules are crafted in sets of 3.
guide.nexustech.lesson.4=The 3x3 array needs daytime, no rain or thunder, and clear sky above every module. Do not overlap arrays. Use the controller to see energy and status. Connect a cable to the controller; poles and modules do not store energy.
guide.nexustech.lesson.5=Electric furnace, crusher and compressor: supply energy, open the machine and insert a valid input. Take the output. The compressor may need multiple items; machine processing recipes are not crafting-table recipes shown here.
guide.nexustech.lesson.6=Breaker: supply FE and a valid pic